Atlas overlay patch 0041: host/download-verbs
Why: the menu of a finished download in the downloads list offers Open, Open With..., Share..., Show in Files,
 a separator and Move to Trash, the last three done by WolOS through the bridge. The verbs are not added to
 DownloadCommands::Command (that would add a case to about fifteen switches of three models and the
 statistics): their ids sit above kMaxValue (static_assert) and DownloadUiContextMenu handles them before
 an id is cast to the enum, so the patch is the menu and the dispatch; the logic is in
 components/atlas_host/download_verbs. The verbs are offered only when the bridge answered its hello; a
 machine without it shows the engine's own menu. Show in folder is worded "Show in Files" (the action is the
 engine's). The row menu view skips the click statistics for an id that is not an engine command. A failure
 is shown in a message box with the words of the desktop; a sheet the person closes says nothing.
Files: chrome/browser/download/BUILD.gn, chrome/browser/download/download_ui_context_menu.h,
 chrome/browser/download/download_ui_context_menu.cc,
 chrome/browser/ui/views/download/download_ui_context_menu_view.cc
Test filter: *DownloadUiContextMenu*:*AtlasHost*; journey atlas-reel.yaml step R07
Rebase risk: M (the menu builders and the switch in GetLabelForCommandId change between releases; the hooks are early returns)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches); BSD-3-Clause (the other hunks)
